      "seed": 1131606459,
      "version": 454,
      "versionNonce": 1692367445,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1795012768333,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Unit tests should be \"stateless\"\n    - each test should be free-standing, and not rely on a test that comes before it, etc.\n    - no data or state should be shared across unit tests.\n\n\nSystem Tests don't have that restriction\n    - you can use \"fixtures\" to share state across tests\n    - usually have a couple different ones\n    - you can do this with MS Test, NUnit, TUnit, and Xunit - in other words, it's a 'thing'\n    - I am just showing XUnit",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Unit tests should be \"stateless\"\n    - each test should be free-standing, and not rely on a test that comes before it, etc.\n    - no data or state should be shared across unit tests.\n\n\nSystem Tests don't have that restriction\n    - you can use \"fixtures\" to share state across tests\n    - usually have a couple different ones\n    - you can do this with MS Test, NUnit, TUnit, and Xunit - in other words, it's a 'thing'\n    - I am just showing XUnit",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
